<title>USA: CCC buys soy-fortified cornmeal for Rwanda, Benin.</title>
<headline>CCC buys soy-fortified cornmeal for Rwanda, Benin.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1996-12-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Commodity Credit Corp of the U.S. Department of Agriculture said it had purchased 4,180 tonnes of soy-fortified cornmeal for export to Rwanda and 360 tonnes for Benin.</p>
<p>The meal was bought from Lauhoff Grain Co of Danville, Il. for between $316.36 and $318.34 per tonne, FOB Jacintoport. Shipment was slated for January 6-February 5, 1997.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk 312-408 8720))</p>
